## 🔬 What We Do

We study how **immune cells shape vascular adaptation** in ischemic disease—and build **AI-powered tools** to decode that complexity.

### Our Research Focus

🩸 **Platelet Immunology**  
Platelets aren't just clotting cells—they're immune regulators. We discovered that platelet C5aR1 controls tissue revascularization via CXCL4 chemokine signaling (*Nature Communications*, 2021).

🤖 **Computational Immunophenotyping**  
We develop ML-based pipelines to analyze 43-color spectral flow cytometry data, profiling 180+ immune subsets in patient blood.

💻 **Open Science Infrastructure**  
All our analysis code is open-source. We believe reproducible science requires reproducible code.

---

## 🧪 Our Approach

| **Wet Lab** | **Dry Lab** |
|-------------|-------------|
| 43-color spectral flow cytometry | Custom R analysis pipelines |
| Single-cell immunophenotyping | Machine learning for cell classification |
| Mouse models of ischemia | Deep learning on coronary angiograms |
| AAV-based gene therapies | Automated quality control & batch correction |

**Translation:** Clinical cohorts (peripheral artery disease, coronary artery disease, aortic stenosis) → Mechanistic insights → Therapeutic targets

